1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,460
Welcome to FIR VisionAI, the u-FIR platform of the Andhra Pradesh Prohibition and Excise Department.

2
00:00:08,510 --> 00:00:14,810
This video walks you through every part of the application, chapter by chapter.

3
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:19,840
Sign in on the Sign In tab with your username and password.

4
00:00:19,890 --> 00:00:28,280
Your role, station, district or state, decides which records you can see, everywhere in the application.

5
00:00:28,330 --> 00:00:37,360
New officers can request an account on the registration tab; an administrator must approve it before it can be used.

6
00:00:37,410 --> 00:00:49,020
After signing in, the Home dashboard shows your name, your jurisdiction scope and your station, with shortcuts to New Case Intake and AI FIR Assistance.

7
00:00:49,070 --> 00:00:58,780
Quick Access has four cards: Existing or Old FIRs, New FIRs, Laws and Sections, and the AI FIR Chatbot.

8
00:00:58,830 --> 00:01:11,900
The count cards show Total Scoped Cases, cases Under Review, Approved FIRs and Pending Drafts, always limited to your jurisdiction. Click a card to open those cases.

9
00:01:11,950 --> 00:01:20,800
The Action Items and Verification Queue lists extracted fields waiting for your sign-off and duplicate entities to review.

10
00:01:20,850 --> 00:01:31,670
Case Management lists every case in your jurisdiction, with tabs for All Cases, Under Review, Approved FIRs, Pending Drafts and Archived.

11
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:40,180
Search by FIR number, contraband, offence or vehicle to find any record, including old FIRs.

12
00:01:40,230 --> 00:01:50,880
Opening a case shows its particulars, the linked accused and vehicles, the original evidence documents, and where each extracted value came from.

13
00:01:50,930 --> 00:02:04,460
From here you can edit fields, replace a document, open the case diary and chargesheet, export the case, or archive it. Every change is recorded in the audit trail.

14
00:02:04,510 --> 00:02:17,620
New Case Intake registers a new FIR. Upload the FIR image or PDF on the Evidence Upload and OCR tab, or type the narrative on the Typed Narrative tab.

15
00:02:17,670 --> 00:02:27,650
The system reads the text and proposes the fields. Review every field, correct anything wrong, and confirm to sign off.

16
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:33,670
The case is registered as Under Review and is never approved automatically.

17
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:49,350
Six stages track the work: upload and OCR, officer review, AI and legal intelligence, investigation drafts, administration, and network intelligence. A failed stage can be retried.

18
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:57,910
If processing fails or is interrupted, press Retry processing; the file does not need to be uploaded again.

19
00:02:57,960 --> 00:03:06,500
Note that the Voice Intake tab is still a placeholder and does not record real audio; use Typed Narrative instead.

20
00:03:06,550 --> 00:03:15,490
FIR Document Extraction shows the document beside the extracted fields and entities, each with a confidence value.

21
00:03:15,540 --> 00:03:26,610
Correct uncertain values before using them. The extracted text is a reading of the original, and the original file always remains the evidence.

22
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:37,090
AI FIR Assistance answers questions only from documents you are allowed to see, and cites the document and page for every statement.

23
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:49,490
Choose a scope: Current FIR, Case plus evidence, FIR plus Law, Knowledge Base, or All authorised. Ask in English, Telugu or Hindi.

24
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:55,770
If the documents do not contain the answer, it says so instead of guessing.

25
00:03:55,820 --> 00:04:09,200
The Knowledge Base holds official laws and sections, circulars and orders, seizure reports, investigation guides, reference material, historical FIR records and approved evidence.

26
00:04:09,250 --> 00:04:23,020
Filter by category, source and status, search inside documents, or browse acts section by section. Source badges show which texts are official and which are unverified.

27
00:04:23,070 --> 00:04:33,530
AI Case Summaries writes cited summaries of historical FIR records in English, Telugu and Hindi, all from the same source text.

28
00:04:33,580 --> 00:04:44,160
Missing details are marked as not available in the source, and records without readable text are flagged for OCR or review instead of being guessed.

29
00:04:44,210 --> 00:04:51,830
A batch can summarise many records at once, with a progress bar, and resumes where it stopped.

30
00:04:51,880 --> 00:05:01,510
Legal Section Assistance suggests sections for a case and shows which ingredients are supported by the facts and which are not yet established.

31
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:12,860
You accept or reject each suggestion. These are decision support, not legal advice, so verify every section against its official text.

32
00:05:12,910 --> 00:05:25,330
Entity Network shows people, vehicles, locations and phone numbers linked across cases. Treat links and risk scores as leads to verify, not findings.

33
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:33,890
The Entity Review Queue lists possible duplicate persons and vehicles; merge them only when they are the same entity.

34
00:05:33,940 --> 00:05:45,160
The Case Diary and Chargesheet generators draft documents from verified case facts. Drafts stay drafts until an officer approves them.

35
00:05:45,210 --> 00:05:56,190
Employee Management, available to district and state officers, provisions officer accounts, approves registration requests and resets passwords.

36
00:05:56,240 --> 00:06:06,830
The Audit Trail records important actions, such as registrations, edits, approvals and document replacements, in a tamper-evident hash chain.

37
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:13,750
The All FIR Folders menu groups cases by offence, by status and by person.

38
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:20,910
Each folder has its own search, and Open Case takes you to the full record with its documents.

39
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:31,420
The headphones button at the bottom right opens the voice assistant on every page. Speak or type in English, Telugu or Hindi.

40
00:06:31,470 --> 00:06:46,290
It explains how to use the application, tells you live counts and FIR status within your jurisdiction, and answers legal questions with citations. It never approves, submits or deletes records.

41
00:06:46,340 --> 00:06:56,570
That completes the tour of FIR VisionAI. For help at any time, open the voice assistant or ask your administrator.
